              <strong class="text-white">Rockwell is a genuinely innovative value brand — best understood as the sibling of WORX under parent company Positec.</strong> Its signature products, especially the Sonicrafter oscillating multi-tool, the Versacut compact circular saw, and the JawHorse clamping workstation, are clever, well-executed tools that deliver real value to DIYers and homeowners. For those specific use cases, Rockwell is an easy recommendation.
            </p>
            <p>
              <strong class="text-white">It is not, however, a professional-grade tool line.</strong> The budget and cordless lines are plastic-heavy and engineered for intermittent homeowner duty, not daily jobsite abuse. The cordless ecosystem is also far smaller than Ryobi's, which matters if you plan to expand across one battery platform for years.
            </p>
            <p class="text-lg border-t border-gray-700 pt-6 mt-6">
              <strong class="text-[#38BDF8]">Bottom Line:</strong> Buy Rockwell for what it does best — the Sonicrafter, the Versacut, the JawHorse, and other standout innovations that punch above their price. <strong class="text-white">If you are a DIYer, weekend warrior, or homeowner who wants smart, affordable tools, Rockwell earns a confident recommendation.</strong> If you are a working professional needing all-day durability, or a buyer committing to a broad cordless ecosystem, step up to Milwaukee, DeWalt, or Ryobi instead. Right tool, right job — and for the right job, Rockwell is well worth a look.
            </p>
